+{"type":"message","id":"8dca841e","parentId":"51b233e1","timestamp":"2026-03-21T18:03:59.750Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Parent conversation handoff summary:\nParent conversation handoff summary\nSummary model: openai-codex/gpt-5.4-mini\nSource items: 79\n\nOverview:\nParent conversation focused on assessing remaining gaps in the Support Bundle Investigator repo against the hiring PDF and PRD v2, after a large Phase 7 implementation landed. The repo already appears to satisfy most core product requirements (CLI-first, local-first, evidence-backed diagnosis, heuristic + AI paths, Markdown/HTML/JSON output, traceability, seeded scenarios), so follow-on work should prioritize reviewer confidence, stronger evals, observability, robustness, and documentation consistency rather than core feature completion.\n\nSettled decisions:\n- The project is effectively past core feature completeness; the remaining work is mainly proof, polish, and confidence-building.\n- The strongest next step is to build a more explicit eval matrix covering scenario, expected top diagnosis, evidence, confidence band, heuristic vs AI results, and spec recommendations.\n- AI-mode behavior is valuable but needs reproducible regression proof via recorded/replayed cassettes or a canonical AI eval corpus.\n- Documentation should be cleaned up so current-complete state is not contradicted by stale roadmap/gap docs.\n- Privacy/sensitive-data assurance should be treated as a differentiating trust feature and validated with tests, especially around secret handling and redaction guidance.\n\nConstraints / must-remember items:\n- README/visible repo surface should make completion obvious; a demo video link is considered a key missing deliverable.\n- Current golden/e2e coverage is narrower than the feature set; several capabilities are unit-tested but under-demonstrated in scenario/e2e form.\n- Observability is currently coarse and should be extended to include retrieval breakdowns, token/cost usage, merge/suppression reasons, and confidence deltas.\n- Need to preserve local-first and no-required-network behavior as the default.\n- Avoid relying on generic LLM summarization; the product must remain evidence- and contradiction-driven.\n- Any changes to docs must avoid confusing reviewers about whether the project is complete or still in progress.\n\nOpen questions:\n- Where is the demo video hosted, and should the repo/README be updated to link it prominently?\n- Which additional seeded scenarios should be added first to cover under-demonstrated investigators (e.g. network policy, node taints/MemoryPressure, Helm release failures)?\n- Should AI evals be added via replayable cassettes in CI, and if so what minimal corpus size is sufficient?\n- What exact observability fields should be added to trace output to make diagnosis, evaluation, and demoing easier?\n- Should stale roadmap/gap content be split into separate completed vs future-work docs, or just re-labeled with a clear historical disclaimer?\n- How should sensitive-data safety be proved end-to-end so reports/prompts demonstrably avoid leaking secret values?\n\nUse this handoff as background context. If it conflicts with the explicit task below or the current repository state, prioritize the explicit task and repo state.\n\nPlan overview:\n{\n  \"goal\": \"Improve evals, observability, and robustness across the Support Bundle Investigator: build a real eval scorecard across all scenarios, add AI replay/cassette evals, expand scenario corpus for newer investigators, enrich trace.json with seed/retrieval/confidence telemetry, add a debug mode with per-finding provenance, add cost/latency/model summaries for AI runs, and add robustness tests for corrupt/partial/oversized bundles, stress/perf benchmarks, and sensitive-data leakage.\",\n  \"totalSteps\": 16,\n  \"stepTitles\": [\n    \"1. Expand eval scorecard: add ghost-service and multi-namespace-retrieval to GOLDEN_EXPECTATIONS\",\n    \"2. Add new scenario fixtures: network-policy-deny and node-taint-memory-pressure\",\n    \"3. Add new scenario fixture: helm-release-failure\",\n    \"4. Build eval scorecard JSON reporter and summary test\",\n    \"5. Wire CassetteRecorder into the LLM execution path for record/replay\",\n    \"6. AI cassette eval test: replay-based golden eval using wired path\",\n    \"7. Enrich InvestigationTrace with seed, retrieval, and confidence telemetry\",\n    \"8. Add per-finding provenance to Finding type and populate in investigators\",\n    \"9. Add AI cost/latency/model summary to trace and report\",\n    \"10. Add --debug CLI flag that emits enriched trace and provenance\",\n    \"11. Robustness: corrupt and partial bundle tests\",\n    \"12. Robustness: oversized bundle guard test\",\n    \"13. Robustness: sensitive-data leakage tests\",\n    \"14. Performance benchmark test for pipeline throughput\",\n    \"15. Wire enriched trace fields into JSON and Markdown report output\",\n    \"16. Final integration pass: build, lint, and full test suite green\"\n  ]\n}\n\nPrevious step 4 (Build eval scorecard JSON reporter and summary test) has been completed and approved.\nFiles changed in the previous step:\n.pi/duet/runs/2026-03-21T16-42-16-431Z-28161f03/cost.json\n.pi/duet/runs/2026-03-21T16-42-16-431Z-28161f03/sessions/continuous/relay-a/2026-03-21T17-33-21-090Z_b7aac197-3cab-4131-a4df-8019588b0f90.jsonl\n.pi/duet/runs/2026-03-21T16-42-16-431Z-28161f03/sessions/continuous/relay-b/2026-03-21T17-37-23-812Z_23a03b14-9632-47c8-9eaf-e9cdd0790ae8.jsonl\n.pi/duet/runs/2026-03-21T16-42-16-431Z-28161f03/state.json\ntest/golden/evaluate.ts\n.pi/duet/runs/2026-03-21T16-42-16-431Z-28161f03/steps/4\ntest/golden/__tests__/scorecard.test.ts\ntest/golden/scorecard.ts\n\nYour session has context from prior steps. The repository may have changed since your last turn.\nBefore making assumptions about file contents, verify the current state of any files you need to modify.\nDo NOT re-read files that are unrelated to the current step.\n\nStep 5: Wire CassetteRecorder into the LLM execution path for record/replay\n{\n  \"id\": \"step-5\",\n  \"title\": \"Wire CassetteRecorder into the LLM execution path for record/replay\",\n  \"description\": \"The existing `CassetteRecorder` in `src/ai/recorder.ts` has record/replay storage but is never integrated into the actual LLM call path, and `loadAIConfig` in `src/ai/config.ts` will not enable AI without a real API key or `SBI_LLM_BACKEND=local`, so replay mode never reaches the AI branch at all. This step fixes both gaps.\\n\\n**0. Make replay mode count as AI-enabled in `src/ai/config.ts`.**\\nModify the `enabled` computation in `loadAIConfig` to add a third enabling condition: `getRecorderMode() === 'replay'`. The current code is:\\n```typescript\\nconst enabled =\\n  requestedProvider === 'openai' &&\\n  !noAi &&\\n  (hasKey || llmBackend === 'local');\\n```\\nChange it to:\\n```typescript\\nconst recorderMode = getRecorderMode();   // import from recorder.ts\\nconst enabled =\\n  requestedProvider === 'openai' &&\\n  !noAi &&\\n  (hasKey || llmBackend === 'local' || recorderMode === 'replay');\\n```\\nAlso set `effectiveApiKey` to `'replay'` (a placeholder) when `recorderMode === 'replay'` and no real key is present, so the `OpenAI` client constructor in `LLMClient` does not throw for a missing key. This is safe because in replay mode the inner client's `investigateSeed` is never called — the `ReplayableLLMClient` wrapper intercepts all calls. Add a unit test in `src/ai/__tests__/config.test.ts` confirming: (a) `SBI_AI_MODE=replay` with no API key yields `enabled: true`, (b) `SBI_AI_MODE=live` with no API key yields `enabled: false` (unchanged), (c) `SBI_AI_MODE=replay` with `noAi: true` still yields `enabled: false`.\\n\\n1. **Create `src/ai/replayable-llm-client.ts`** — a wrapper class `ReplayableLLMClient` that implements the same interface as `LLMClient` (specifically `investigateSeed(system, user): Promise<AIFindingResponse>` and `generateText(system, user): Promise<string>`). Constructor takes: `inner: LLMClient`, `recorder: CassetteRecorder`, and `seedResolver: (system: string, user: string) => { seedId: string; seedCategory: string }`. Behavior per mode:\\n   - **`record`**: calls `inner.investigateSeed()`, then calls `recorder.record()` with the seed identity and response, returns the real response.\\n   - **`replay`**: calls `recorder.replay()` with the seed identity. If a cassette exists, returns `{ findings: cassette.response.findings, rawResponse: cassette.response.rawResponse }`. If missing, returns `{ findings: [], rawResponse: undefined }` (graceful degradation, no throw). Logs a warning for missing cassettes. **Never calls `inner.investigateSeed()`** — no network request is made.\\n   - **`live`**: delegates directly to `inner` with no recording.\\n   For `generateText`, always delegates to `inner` in record/live modes; in replay mode returns an empty string (HyDE is non-critical and must not make network calls).\\n\\n2. **Add a `seedResolver` helper** in the same file that extracts seed identity from the prompt text. The user prompt built by `buildInvestigationPrompt` contains the seed hypothesis and source — parse the seed ID and category from a `<!-- seed:... -->` HTML comment that we'll inject into the prompt. Alternatively (simpler), change `investigateWithAI` to pass seed metadata alongside the LLM call so the wrapper can key cassettes correctly.\\n\\n3. **Update `investigateWithAI` in `src/investigators/ai-investigator.ts`** — change the per-seed loop to pass `seed.id` and `seed.category` to the LLM call. The cleanest approach: add an optional `currentSeed?: InvestigationSeed` field to `AIInvestigatorDeps` or introduce a `setSeedContext(seed)` method on `ReplayableLLMClient`. Before each `llmClient.investigateSeed()` call, set the current seed so the wrapper knows which cassette key to use.\\n\\n4. **Update `analyzeBundlePipeline` in `src